            <ArticleTitle>The electrodiagnostic evaluation of neck pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>429-38, viii</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.pmr.2011.02.012</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Electrodiagnostic studies play an important role in the evaluation of radiculopathy. This article reviews the use of standard nerve conduction studies, late responses, evoked potentials, and needle electrode examination in the electrodiagnostic evaluation of neck pain.</AbstractText>
